      "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe gateway's forwarding `reqwest` client sets `TCP_USER_TIMEOUT` to 30 s on Linux by default. If an engine stops reading a forwarded request body for over 30 s (e.g. busy with a burst of long prompts), the send is aborted and the router returns 500 regardless of `request_timeout_secs`. Same fix as #45696 for `sgl-router`.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `sgl-model-gateway/src/app_context.rs`: disable `tcp_user_timeout` on the forwarding client on the targets where reqwest sets it. `request_timeout_secs` still bounds a request.\n\n## Testing\n\nEnd to end with a worker that reads no POST body for 40 s:\n\n| Router build | Result |\n|---|---|\n| main | 500 after 30 s |\n| this PR | 200 after 40 s |\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n",
